T in __all__.\n\n2. Spec faithfulness - StreamIdObservation. Field set, ordering, types, and __post_init__ invariants exactly match spec 52. parsed_id helper returns (int, int). Negative-value rejection coverage is complete. stream_id form validation is correct.\n\n3. Spec faithfulness - GrowthWindowConfig. Same as #2 for the four fields. boundary_inclusive must be exactly bool (type check, not truthy).\n\n4. Spec faithfulness - compute_stream_id_growth_in_window. Window boundary semantics (strict-> default, inclusive opt-in) match spec. Stream-name filter applies after future-observation rejection. Distinctness counted on literal string. Future observation always raises regardless of position. observations parameter must be tuple, not any iterable. stream_name parameter is keyword-only.\n\n5. Out-of-band requirement compliance per 05 spec. No XLEN literal anywhere in beta source (rg \"XLEN\" -> 0; rg \"xlen\" -> 0). The function signature consumes a snapshot-of-observations rather than calling Redis itself.\n\n6. Hard-exclusion compliance. No subprocess. No file I/O. No network. No Redis. No legacy import. No environment variable read. No reliance on the 2E1.A subprocess adapter. No reliance on the 2E1.B record contract. No reliance on the 2E1.C.alpha liveness domain (rg \"trainer_liveness\" -> 0). No live trainer call. No model / checkpoint loading. No GPU code. No async. No clock read. No numpy. No torch. No tensorflow. Verify by re-running the forbidden-token grep over the beta source and test trees.\n\n7. END_FILE marker hygiene. rg \"^END_FILE:\" returns zero hits across both source and test trees. py_compile succeeds for all 16 Python files (re-run via Bash; do not modify any file).\n\n8. Test coverage. Each rubric in spec 53 maps to at least one test. Note any missing case (especially boundary at lo, future-observation at end of tuple, generator rejection, bool-as-int rejection in window_ms, mixed-stream filter then distinctness).\n\n9. Cross-symbol isolation. liveness_stream_growth must not import any symbol from v2.backend.app.domain.trainer_liveness (alpha) or v2.backend.app.domain.trainer_parity (2E1.B) or v2.backend.app.adapters.trainer (2E1.A). Verify by recursive grep.\n\n10. Documentation alignment. Field rationales documented inline (e.g. why distinctness on literal string, why filter after future-rejection). Implementation report (57) accurately reflects authored state.\n\n11. Safety boundaries adherence. Spec 54 forbidden-action list is fully respected. No live trading enablement. LIVE TRADING: BLOCKED is preserved.\n\n12. Adversarial probes. Try at least: (a) StreamIdObservation with whitespace-only stream_name -> raises; (b) StreamIdObservation with stream_id 'abc-0' -> raises; (c) GrowthWindowConfig with window_ms=True -> raises (bool is int subclass; spec demands type rejection); (d) compute_stream_id_growth_in_window with observations=[] (list) -> raises observations_not_tuple; (e) compute_stream_id_growth_in_window with future-stamped observation in non-matching stream -> raises (future check before stream filter); (f) compute_stream_id_growth_in_window with positional stream_name -> raises TypeError.\n\nEmit outputs (BEGIN_FILE / END_FILE blocks - these are Markdown files):\n\nclaude_worklog/phase2_core_rebuild/trainer_gpu_parity_impl/60_2E1C_BETA_CODEX_REVIEW.md\n- Heading 'Phase 2E1.C.beta - Codex Review'.\n- One section per rubric item with PASS / FAIL / WARN, evidence pointer (file path and line range or marker), and remediation ask if FAIL.\n- Section 'Adversarial coverage probes' listing the additional cases Codex tried and their outcomes.\n- Final marker line: PHASE2E1C_BETA_TRAINER_PARITY_IMPL_CODEX_PASS or PHASE2E1C_BETA_TRAINER_PARITY_IMPL_CODEX_FAIL.\n\nclaude_worklog/phase2_core_rebuild/trainer_gpu_parity_impl/61_2E1C_BETA_CODEX_GO_NO_GO.md\n- Exactly one line: PHASE2E1C_BETA_TRAINER_PARITY_IMPL_CODEX_PASS or PHASE2E1C_BETA_TRAINER_PARITY_IMPL_CODEX_FAIL. No other content.\n\nSafety guarantees. Do not modify any file under v2/backend/. Do not modify legacy. Do not commit. Do not push. Do not run any subprocess other than pytest (read-only re-run is allowed for verification), python -m py_compile, python -c, and grep / rg. Do not start the legacy trainer venv. Do not import any legacy module. Do not access Redis. Do not access network. Do not read .env. Do not enable live trading.\n\nOn FAIL, the supervisor opens a remediation task under REQ_0007 autofix scope before re-implementation. Codex must NOT silently fix the failure inside this review task.",
