uCoin/CoinAPI evidence, liquidity/volume/volatility/open-interest/freshness scores, feature completeness, manual overrides, observed/training/paper/shadow/live-blocked state reason.\n\n6. Risk-decision element coverage. The 'Risk-decision explanation source survey' covers every element REQ_0009 'Trade/risk explanation' lists for the risk side: signal reason, risk gateway result, sizing reason, stale signal check, duplicate check, exposure check, drawdown check, live gate status, execution mode (paper/shadow/live-blocked), final decision reason.\n\n7. Trade-decision element coverage. The 'Trade open/close/hedge/block explanation source survey' covers the open/close/hedge/block transitions and references the corresponding execution and trader modules.\n\n8. Audit-timeline coverage. The 'Audit-timeline source survey' identifies a write-once chain owner (likely v2/backend/app/domain/governance/audit_chain.py if present) or marks a P0 GAP.\n\n9. Gap matrix completeness. All seven tables (A\u2013G) are present in 06. Each gap has a severity (P0/P1/P2) and a proposed owner sub-phase that exists in the Phase 2H breakdown.\n\n10. Cross-cutting concerns. The 'Cross-cutting concerns' section in 06 identifies at least one cross-stage concern (typical example: a missing decision_id minting that affects risk + execution + audit at once). If no concerns are identified, FAIL UNLESS 05 evidence demonstrates none exist.\n\n11. Suggested 2H.A.1 / 2H.A.2 / 2H.A.3 scope. The final section of 06 distills the gap matrix into the three follow-up documentation sub-phases consistent with the Phase 2H breakdown.\n\n12. Forbidden-token grep. Run rg with case-sensitive matching across the entire claude_worklog/phase2_core_rebuild/decision_explainability/ subtree for: redis, aioredis, redis.asyncio, subprocess, os.system, os.popen, pty, socket, urllib, requests, httpx, aiohttp, torch, tensorflow, numpy, cuda, legacy_reference, /home/wali/Desktop/AI BOT, BINANCE_API_KEY, BINANCE_API_SECRET, live_