ivenessAlert and reason constants. alert_code constraint enforced. _ALLOWED_LIVENESS_REASONS contains exactly six reasons: prediction_age_exceeds_sla, gpu_batch_age_exceeds_sla, proposal_age_exceeds_sla, prediction_stream_zero_growth, prediction_worker_dead, fatal_log_signature_observed. Unknown / duplicate / empty reasons rejected. observation_ts_ms == snapshot.observation_ts_ms enforced.\n\n5. Spec faithfulness - evaluator (post-autofix six-rule version). The six rules are implemented in this exact evaluation order: prediction_age_exceeds_sla, gpu_batch_age_exceeds_sla, proposal_age_exceeds_sla, prediction_stream_zero_growth, prediction_worker_dead, fatal_log_signature_observed. The prediction_worker_dead rule is evaluated INDEPENDENTLY of the zero-stream-growth branch (a non-zero prediction_stream_id_growth must NOT suppress the worker-dead alert; verify by re-reading evaluator.py:48-57 and the targeted test test_evaluator_prediction_worker_dead.py). None-handling for missing timestamps (never-emitted case) is correct: prediction-age reason does NOT fire when last_prediction_ts_ms is None; the zero-stream-growth reason still covers the never-emitted case when parent is alive. Strict > comparison for SLA boundaries (equal-to-SLA returns None). now_ms < observation_ts_ms raises. now_ms < 0 raises. Returns None when no reasons fire. Returns LivenessAlert with deterministic reason ordering otherwise.\n\n6. Out-of-band requirement compliance per 05 spec. No write to legacy Redis (verified by grep). No restart of the legacy trainer (no subprocess calls, no os.kill, no process management). No XLEN-style growth measurement (the field name is prediction_stream_id_growth and the evaluator treats it as already-measured-over-window; the consumption order matches the timezone-aware corrected approach). No emission to V2_REDIS_PREFIX in this phase.\n\n7. Hard-exclusion compliance. No subprocess. No file I/O. No network. No Redis. No legacy import. No environment variable read.