ing across the entire claude_worklog/phase2_core_rebuild/frontend_design/ subtree for: redis, aioredis, subprocess, os.system, legacy_reference, /home/wali/Desktop/AI BOT, BINANCE_API_KEY, BINANCE_API_SECRET, live_trading_enabled = true. Every count MUST be zero. Any non-zero count is FAIL.\n\n10. No live behavior. Neither spec mentions enabling live trading, mutating legacy, writing Redis, or deploying. The LIVE TRADING: BLOCKED semantics are preserved.\n\n11. Implementation surface clarity. Each spec names the exact module path the next-phase implementer (2F.B.0 / 2F.B.1) will create and the exact filename per kind/primitive. The token spec exports interface signature is Readonly<Record<string, string|number>>; the primitive spec test file is one test file per primitive under v2/frontend/tests/unit/motion/.\n\n12. Adversarial probes. Try at least: (a) does the spec accidentally introduce light-mode-first chrome? (b) does the spec leave any animation token without a duration or easing reference? (c) does the spec require any feature that depends on legacy Redis or exchange APIs? (d) is StatusPulseIndicator the only infinite-iteration primitive, and does it state a frequency cap?\n\nEmit outputs (BEGIN_FILE / END_FILE blocks - these are Markdown files):\n\nclaude_worklog/phase2_core_rebuild/frontend_design/14_2FA1_CODEX_REVIEW.md\n- Heading 'Phase 2F.A.1 - Codex Review'.\n- One section per rubric item with PASS / FAIL / WARN, evidence pointer (file path and section), and remediation ask if FAIL.\n- Section 'Adversarial coverage probes' listing the additional cases Codex tried and their outcomes.\n- Final marker line: PHASE2FA1_DESIGN_SPEC_CODEX_PASS or PHASE2FA1_DESIGN_SPEC_CODEX_FAIL.\n\nclaude_worklog/phase2_core_rebuild/frontend_design/15_2FA1_CODEX_GO_NO_GO.md\n- Exactly one line: PHASE2FA1_DESIGN_SPEC_CODEX_PASS or PHASE2FA1_DESIGN_SPEC_CODEX_FAIL. No other content.\n\nSafety guarantees. Do not modify any file under v2/. Do not modify legacy. Do not commit. Do 